WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.816 --> 00:00:08.376
Smiling naturally in front of a camera is hard for everyone.

2
00:00:08.712 --> 00:00:14.064
The secret to looking your best is smiling with your eyes and whole face, not just your mouth.

3
00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:20.496
One to two months before the wedding, practice loosening your mouth muscles in the mirror with 'ah-eh-ee-oh-oo,'

4
00:00:20.832 --> 00:00:24.720
and practice a bright smile that shows about eight upper teeth.

5
00:00:25.056 --> 00:00:33.528
During the shoot, tuck your chin slightly instead of lifting it, since lifting makes the face look bigger, and keep a warm gaze as if looking past the lens at your beloved child.

6
00:00:33.864 --> 00:00:42.936
Remember the mirror effect too — if you smile brightly first, guests and the photographer pick up on that positive energy, leading to the best results.

7
00:00:43.272 --> 00:00:48.888
For a bright smile that lasts forever in your photos, practice loosening your muscles and smiling ahead of time.
